---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MethodMotion from "../components/MethodMotion.astro";
import { methods } from "../data/methods";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section class="home-hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="category">Engineering method layer for Codex.</p>
      <h1>Method as exponent. <span>Not machinery.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Servotab changes how Codex plans, builds, debugs, reviews, and verifies
        repository work. Clear changes stay direct. Higher-risk work receives
        stronger method and fresh evidence.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="action action-primary" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
        <a class="action action-secondary" href="/methods">Explore methods</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <MethodMotion />
  </section>

  <section class="home-section shell" aria-labelledby="two-paths-heading">
    <div class="section-lead">
      <p class="section-index">01 / Two paths</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="two-paths-heading">Direct when clear. Deliberate when risk demands it.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Method follows the repository task. It never replaces the work or
          turns every request into the same process.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="path-grid">
      <article class="path-item">
        <span class="path-number">path / direct</span>
        <span class="path-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Clear local change</h3>
        <p>
          A bounded, reversible edit stays on the shortest useful path: inspect
          the relevant source, make the change, run the focused check, and close.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="path-item">
        <span class="path-number">path / method</span>
        <span class="path-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <h3>Risky repository change</h3>
        <p>
          A selected method adds the planning, diagnosis, isolation, review, or
          verification the task genuinely needs—bounded to the real risk.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section shell" aria-labelledby="promises-heading">
    <div class="section-lead">
      <p class="section-index">02 / Product promises</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="promises-heading">Controlled leverage, without process theatre.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Four behaviors hold the line between useful method and unnecessary machinery.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="promise-list">
      <div class="promise-row"><span>direct</span><strong>Clear changes stay direct.</strong></div>
      <div class="promise-row"><span>method</span><strong>Risk brings stronger method.</strong></div>
      <div class="promise-row"><span>closure</span><strong>Fresh evidence closes the loop.</strong></div>
      <div class="promise-row"><span>scope</span><strong>The requested outcome stays whole.</strong></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell" aria-labelledby="methods-preview-heading">
    <div class="method-preview">
      <div>
        <h2 id="methods-preview-heading">A small method, placed precisely.</h2>
        <p>
          Servotab’s candidate method set spans design, execution, debugging,
          review, verification, isolation, delegation, and closure. The router
          chooses depth proportionately; explicit method names remain available
          when a person wants precise control.
        </p>
        <div class="method-line" aria-label="Candidate Servotab methods">
          {methods.map((method) => <span>{method.name}</span>)}
        </div>
      </div>
      <a class="action action-secondary" href="/methods">See all methods</a>
    </div>

    <div class="availability-note">
      <span>availability</span>
      <p>
        Servotab is being prepared for directory submission and is not currently
        listed in the OpenAI plugin directory. Source-checkout installation remains
        available in the <a href="/docs#availability-heading">Docs</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
